# Go packages blocked from auto-upgrade (require manual migration).
#
# Format: module/path  # BLOCKER: <substantive reason>
#
# The BLOCKER convention is enforced by .ci/scripts/quality/check-go-deps.sh
# (see parse_blockered_list in .ci/scripts/lib/blocker-validator.sh): each
# line needs a 30+ char reason that does not match the banned-phrase list.
#
# Minor/patch updates for non-blocked packages will fail CI. Major updates
# are always reported but never auto-upgraded regardless of this list.

# Docker SDK — v26+ has major API and package path changes
github.com/docker/docker  # BLOCKER: v26+ breaks client.NewClientWithOpts signature and renames several packages; requires rewrite of renet docker client
github.com/docker/go-connections  # BLOCKER: v0.7.0 removed sockets.DialPipe which docker/docker v25 still uses; pinned to v0.6.0 until docker SDK upgrade

# go-landlock — sandbox isolation primitive (security-critical)
github.com/landlock-lsm/go-landlock  # BLOCKER: v0.9.0 is a 0.x minor that can change the Landlock config API; this gates repo-sandbox isolation, so adoption needs sandbox-behavior validation on a live cluster before bumping

# BLOCKER: kubelet is consumed for exactly one thing, the stable pluginregistration/v1
# types (GetInfo / NotifyRegistrationStatus), which have not changed. Taking v0.36.x buys
# nothing and costs three things: it REQUIRES an untagged protobuf pseudo-version
# (v1.36.12-0.20260120151049-f2248ac996af — upstream k8s 1.36 ships against an unreleased
# protobuf commit; pinning protobuf to the tagged v1.36.11 drags kubelet down to
# v0.36.0-alpha.2), it forces the go directive from 1.25 to 1.26, and it breaks the
# generated RegistrationServer interface (needs UnimplementedRegistrationServer embedded),
# which means editing the CSI registration path while that path is under active
# investigation for the #87 staging bug. Revisit once protobuf v1.36.12 is tagged and a
# kubelet release requires the tagged version.
k8s.io/kubelet

